/-! # The quotient of a period curve by the image of a superlattice

For an upper half-plane parameter τ, the period curve of `ℤτ + ℤ` with the cyclic subgroup
generated by the image of `1/N` has, as its vendored iterated Vélu quotient, a curve whose
j-invariant is `j(Nτ)`. The proof reads the quotient map as a map of function fields, lifts it to
the universal covers, and computes its kernel: the lift is `z ↦ αz + c` and the preimage of the
subgroup is `ℤτ + ℤ(1/N)`, so the quotient lattice is homothetic to `ℤNτ + ℤ`. -/

